   "evidence": "Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Action/Defs.lean:499 `lemma inv_smul_smul (g : G) (a : \u03b1) : g\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 g \u2022 a = a`; :502 `lemma smul_inv_smul (g : G) (a : \u03b1) : g \u2022 g\u207b\u00b9 \u2022 a = a`; Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Action/Basic.lean:51 `protected lemma MulAction.injective (g : \u03b1) : Function.Injective (g \u2022 \u00b7 : \u03b2 \u2192 \u03b2)` (and :47 `MulAction.bijective`, :59 `smul_left_cancel`). `SubstGroup R` is a new type, so the instance creates no diamond with existing actions on `R\u27e6X\u27e7`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Factorization/Evolution/BetaFunction.lean",
   "fix": "Register `instance : MulAction (SubstGroup R) R\u27e6X\u27e7 := { smul := transformBeta, one_smul := transformBeta_one, mul_smul := transformBeta_mul }` and delete the three lemmas in favour of `inv_smul_smul F \u03b2`, `smul_inv_smul F \u03b2` and `MulAction.injective F`; if the named forms are kept for readability, prove each as a one-liner from those.",
   "issue": "`transformBeta_one` (line 120) and `transformBeta_mul` (line 126) are literally the `one_smul`/`mul_smul` axioms of `MulAction (SubstGroup R) R\u27e6X\u27e7`, but no instance is declared, so `transformBeta_inv_transformBeta` (132), `transformBeta_transformBeta_inv` (138) and `transformBeta_injective` (145) re-prove generic Mathlib lemmas and the rest of the action API (bijectivity, surjectivity, `smul_left_cancel`, `inv_smul_eq_iff`, orbits) is unavailable.",
   "line": 132
  }
